            <ArticleTitle>Left ventricular mass: myxoma or thrombus?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>95-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/0971-9784.148329</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patient with embolic episode should always be evaluated for cardiac mass. Mass in left ventricular can be a myxoma or thrombus even in a normal functioning heart. In either case, mobile mass with embolic potential should be surgically resected.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
